        "root_concepts": "[ecology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Carrying capacity K = autoscaling ceiling enforced by resource constraints\n  dN/dt = rN(K-N)/K: growth decelerates as utilization approaches capacity\n  Unlike autoscaling, K is not configurable — it's set by food, space, predators\n  Allee effects: positive feedback at low density — below threshold, population collapses\n  → Analogous to minimum viable traffic for a service to stay warm/healthy"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ECOLOGY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-ECOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:05-ecology, git-history:biology:05-ecology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/05-ECOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[ecology]",
        "current_path": "biology/05-ECOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:ecology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ecology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Predator-prey (Lotka-Volterra) = load balancer oscillation\n  Prey = requests; predator = processing capacity\n  More prey → predator grows → prey suppressed → predator starves → prey recovers\n  Neutrally stable cycles in the basic model (like undamped LC circuit oscillation)\n  Real systems: damped or limit cycles — additional feedback terms (prey refuge,\n    prey switching) add damping\n  → Same math as SIR epidemiological model: dS/dt, dI/dt, dR/dt"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ECOLOGY.md#014",
      "path": [
        "05-ECOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:05-ecology, git-history:biology:05-ecology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/05-ECOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[ecology]",
        "current_path": "biology/05-ECOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:ecology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ecology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Food web = directed dependency graph with energy as the flow metric\n  Nodes: species; edges: trophic interactions (who eats whom)\n  Connectance C = L/S² (link density); empirical food webs: C ≈ 0.05-0.15\n  Stability: May (1972) showed random networks destabilize with more connections\n  Real food webs stable via: compartmentalization (modules), weak links (damping),\n    asymmetric interaction strengths\n  → Parallels: microservice dependency graph; weak coupling = stable architecture"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ECOLOGY.md#015",
      "path": [
        "05-ECOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:05-ecology, git-history:biology:05-ecology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/05-ECOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[ecology]",
        "current_path": "biology/05-ECOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:ecology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ecology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Keystone species = single point of failure (SPOF) in ecosystem architecture\n  Pisaster sea star (<1% of intertidal biomass) → remove → 15 species lost → mussel monoculture\n  Keystone identifies fragility in the dependency graph that biomass alone doesn't reveal\n  → Like identifying critical path nodes in a distributed system"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ECOLOGY.md#016",
      "path": [
        "05-ECOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:05-ecology, git-history:biology:05-ecology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/05-ECOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[ecology]",
        "current_path": "biology/05-ECOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:ecology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ecology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "05 - Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Trophic cascade = indirect effects propagating through the dependency graph\n  Wolves (added) → elk (suppressed) → willows (recovered) → beavers (returned) → hydrology (changed)\n  n-hop indirect effects dominate; direct effects are the minority of ecological impact\n  → Like a service outage propagating through a dependency chain\n```"
    },
